575-9764-44e144045f82" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455442 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 11 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 7 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=6 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=-7 \\\\ -3{x}_{3}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=2.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}-2(2)=-7\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=2$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(3)+2=6\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have ${x}_{1}=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455505 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186455386 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455505 #edb/ref 1069 "q-76054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455505 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455505 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the coordinates of the vector $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ then what is the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455505 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e3764343-10e9-5a7d-b034-e095faf7f51c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455505 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find ${x}_{1}$,  ${x}_{2}$, and ${x}_{3}$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =x \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 15 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom this, we get the system with the augmented matrix $M$, which we reduce using Gaussian elimination: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M= & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{2} \\\\ ∼ & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3 & 15 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -9 & -27\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}=15 \\\\ -9{x}_{3}=-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=3.$ Substituting this into the second   equation yields\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}+3(3)=15\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=3.\n$$\n\n Finally,  by substituting ${x}_{2}=3$ and ${x}_{3}=3$ into the first equation we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3+3=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=3+3+3=9.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455516 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186455531 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186455516 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3120d902-59cf-52